    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0194" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119 P 43/956: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-22T13:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 22, 1918—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 22—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. From Grew. I have been informed that
                    the French Government is taking the necessary step to place the Hotel Crillon at
                        <pb facs="0195" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/> our disposal. Ambassador Sharp is attending to all of these negotiations
                    and will no doubt report direct on terms thereof. We are making satisfactory
                    progress with physical organization of offices in quarters previously occupied
                    by Red Cross at 4 Place de la Concorde.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
